## The day Marienbad went world-class

On **24 July 2021** in Fuzhou, the UNESCO World Heritage Committee raised its hand at its 44th session for an inscription West Bohemia had awaited for over a decade: **The Great Spa Towns of Europe** became World Heritage. Among the eleven towns from seven countries — from Bath in England to Montecatini in Italy — three are Czech: **Karlovy Vary, Mariánské Lázně and Františkovy Lázně**.

In September 2026 the whole region marks the fifth anniversary with a campaign tellingly named **"5 let světoví"** — five years world-class — and the three-day celebrations open in Mariánské Lázně. Before we get to the programme, it is worth recalling what we are actually celebrating.

## Why spa towns, of all things

UNESCO does not inscribe individual buildings; it inscribes **values**. With the spa towns, that value is a phenomenon Europe gave the world: towns built around springs, where treatment merged with architecture, parks, culture and social life into a single whole — the **therapeutic landscape**.

Mariánské Lázně is the textbook example: the colonnade and spring pavilions flow into parks, the parks into forest promenades, and the promenades into a landscape that is itself part of the cure. That is why the inscription covers more than the historic centre — what is protected is precisely that continuous landscape in which people have walked, drunk and breathed for two hundred years. We describe it in detail in [Why Marienbad is UNESCO](/en/magazine/why-marienbad-unesco) and on the [UNESCO](/en/unesco) page.

## What has changed in five years

The inscription was not a finishing line but a commitment. Five years on, the town clearly takes it seriously:

- **Monument care has accelerated** — from the restoration of colonnade structures to sensitive renovations of the spa houses; building and repair here must preserve the value the inscription was granted for
- **The town gained climatic spa status (2023)** — as if to prove the "therapeutic landscape" is no stage set: the local air has since been an officially recognised healing resource; more on the [climate therapy](/en/climate-therapy) page
- **Culture is growing** — the [country's oldest symphony orchestra](/en/magazine/zapadocesky-symfonicky-orchestr) is heading for its 205th anniversary with a new chief conductor, and the colonnade lives with concerts from spring to autumn
- **The world has noticed** — guests now come "for the UNESCO brand" too; three inscribed towns in one region are a magnet with no parallel anywhere

## The celebrations, 11–13 September 2026: three days, three towns

The Karlovy Vary Region has prepared a three-day programme for the anniversary — each day in a different one of the three inscribed towns.

### Friday 11 September — Mariánské Lázně

The celebrations **open right here**:

- **9:00–15:00** — the **Heritage Forum** conference on caring for World Heritage
- **18:00** — launch of the **Great Spa Times** newspaper
- **19:00–21:00** — the **opening celebration**

### Saturday 12 September — Karlovy Vary

An all-day forum in the UNESCO park, a concert at the Imperial Spa at 6 pm and the **VARY°ZÁŘÍ** evening programme.

### Sunday 13 September — Františkovy Lázně

Landmark tours, youth forum presentations and a lecture on the history of the railway that once linked the spa triangle.

The current, continuously updated programme is on the regional website: [kr-karlovarsky.cz/5letsvetovi](https://www.kr-karlovarsky.cz/5letsvetovi).

## A September like few before it

The anniversary also falls in the weeks when the town offers most: **European Heritage Days** (7–20 Sept) open buildings normally closed to the public, on 12 September the **Chopin House and the Anglican Chapel** open their doors, and the same day brings the **closing colonnade concert of the season**.

In other words: if you have ever wondered when to visit Mariánské Lázně for the first time — **the second week of September 2026 is the answer**.

## Practical information

- **Celebration dates:** 11–13 September 2026 (Mariánské Lázně opens on Friday 11 Sept)
- **Programme:** [kr-karlovarsky.cz/5letsvetovi](https://www.kr-karlovarsky.cz/5letsvetovi)
